fastent release notes
=====================

This file contains user-visible changes for each release.  For a
complete source-level history, see the ChangeLog.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unreleased

  Extended statistics (-e / --extended)
  -------------------------------------

  A new -e / --extended flag adds min-entropy (H-infinity, the
  NIST SP 800-90B measure), collision entropy (H2) and the index of
  coincidence, a poker test (16-bin nibble chi-square with 15 degrees
  of freedom), variance and standard deviation, redundancy, the
  distinct-symbol count, and the most / least common symbol.  The new
  values are appended to the default, terse CSV, JSON, and recursive
  output, and --sort-by accepts the new columns (min-entropy,
  collision, ic, poker, variance, redundancy, distinct).  Without -e
  the output is byte-for-byte the classic format.  All extended
  quantities are derived at finalisation from the histogram and the
  running sums, so they add no per-byte cost and stay bit-identical
  across hosts and thread counts.  -log2 is taken via the existing
  faithfully-rounded entropy term, so no libm log enters.

  Annotated report (--annotate)
  -----------------------------

  --annotate (which implies -e) renders an interpretive table: each
  metric is shown with its value, a p-value or z-score where defined,
  a PASS / WEAK / FAIL / N/A badge, and a one-line explanation,
  closing with a headline verdict that names the weakest signal.
  Badge colour follows --color.  Not supported with -r.

  Internal
  --------

  The chi-square upper-tail closed form is generalised to any odd
  degrees of freedom (fastent_chisq_tail_df); the df=1 and df=255
  paths are unchanged and bit-identical.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.1 (May 2026)

  New analyse variants
  --------------------

  AArch64 NEON (mandatory baseline) and ARMv7-A NEON (optional;
  configure picks -mfpu=neon with softfp / hardfp ABI matching the
  rest of the build).  AArch64 SVE2 with variable vector length,
  selected at runtime when HWCAP2_SVE2 is set (Linux), elf_aux_info
  reports it (FreeBSD), or sysctl hw.optional.arm.FEAT_SVE2 is 1
  (macOS).  AVX-512 BITALG variant (VPOPCNTB-driven bit-mode body);
  hosts without BITALG fall back to the F + BW base tier.
  WebAssembly SIMD128 variant driven by wasm_i32x4_dot_i16x8 and
  wasm_i8x16_popcnt, enabled by -msimd128 at configure time.

  I/O backends
  ------------

  --io={auto,mmap,stream,uring} replaces the binary --no-mmap toggle
  (kept as an alias for --io=stream).

  --io=uring on Linux 5.1+ pipelines four 2 MiB reads through
  io_uring via raw __NR_io_uring_setup / __NR_io_uring_enter (no
  liburing dependency).  Falls back to stream on older kernels
  unless the user explicitly requested uring.

  --io=uring on Windows Vista+ uses an IOCP pipeline of four
  overlapped ReadFiles drained through GetQueuedCompletionStatus,
  giving the same four-in-flight latency hide on NVMe cold-cache
  workloads.  The flag name stays "uring" for cross-platform
  symmetry; ENOSYS under --with-windows-target=win95.

  Histogram visualisation
  -----------------------

  -H / --histogram renders a terminal block plot of the byte (or
  bit) distribution.  Eight-level Unicode block glyphs (U+2581 to
  U+2588) by default; on DOS / Win95 / Win98 consoles fastent emits
  single-byte CP 437 glyphs (0xDC, 0xDB) instead so the bars render
  natively under the OEM code page.  ASCII '#' / ' ' for redirected
  output.

  --color=auto|always|never paints control / ASCII / high-bit bytes
  in dim grey / default / accent.  ANSI escapes on POSIX terminals,
  SetConsoleTextAttribute on Win32 (works on Win95+ without
  ANSI.SYS), BIOS-attribute writes via DJGPP <conio.h> textcolor on
  MS-DOS.

  --log toggles a logarithmic Y axis, useful for sparse or
  long-tailed distributions.

  Recursive mode
  --------------

  -r / --recursive walks a directory and emits one row per regular
  file.  CSV by default (path,unit,samples,entropy,chi_square,
  p_exceed,mean,monte_carlo_pi,serial_correlation), JSON under
  --json (array of objects under "files").  Walk follows symlinks
  only at the root, not during recursion.

  --sort-by=COL[:asc|:desc] sorts the rows before printing.  COL is
  one of path, samples, entropy, chisq, mean, pi, scc; the default
  direction is descending for numeric columns and ascending for
  path.

  Platforms
  ---------

  WebAssembly via emscripten with -sSTANDALONE_WASM, for both
  wasm32 and wasm64 (-sMEMORY64); -msimd128 enables 128-bit SIMD
  codegen.  The wasm64 binary needs a runtime with the memory64
  proposal enabled (wasmtime -W memory64, node --experimental-
  wasm-memory64).

  MS-DOS via DJGPP with CWSDPMI bundled into the .exe so there is
  no separate CWSDPMI.EXE needed at runtime.  Native console
  histogram uses CP 437 block glyphs + BIOS-attribute colour.

  Windows 95 / 98 / Me via --with-windows-target=win95: narrow path
  API, PE subsystem 4.0, import table limited to kernel32 + msvcrt.
  Threads and IOCP are disabled on this target.

  Linux on additional architectures added to the smoke matrix:
  alpha, sparc64, sparc, m68k, hppa, arc, sh4 (all glibc-static).

  OpenBSD pledge(2) support: "stdio rpath" until the input is open,
  then "stdio" for the analysis phase.

  Build system
  ------------

  Platform port layer:  port-cpu, port-io, port-term, port-os,
  port-thread, port-walk.  Each port has a header plus
  per-platform implementations (POSIX, Win32, DJGPP) gated by
  arch / OS macros at the top of the .c file.  The main analysis
  and CLI code no longer carries platform #ifdefs.

  Win32 native build now ships UTF-8 paths and console: argv is
  reconstructed from GetCommandLineW with an MSVCRT-compatible
  splitter, the console code page is set to CP_UTF8, and all path
  arguments are routed through _wopen / CreateFileW.

  Thread pool gains a Win32 backend (CreateThread + SRWLOCK +
  CONDITION_VARIABLE, Vista+).  fastent therefore supports -j on
  native Windows builds without WSL.

  Output determinism
  ------------------

  Shannon entropy is now computed via a double-double Horner
  expansion of log2(1+r) with a 128-entry reciprocal table and a
  split-domain branch at p = 0.5 (Sterbenz-exact q = 1 - p).
  Faithfully rounded.  The result is bit-identical across libc /
  FPU implementations, where the previous libm log2 path varied by
  ~1 ULP across hosts.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.0 (May 2026)

  Initial release.

  Tests reported
  --------------

  Shannon entropy, chi-square statistic with tail probability,
  arithmetic mean, Monte Carlo value of pi, and serial correlation
  coefficient.  Byte mode by default; bit mode under -b (two-bin
  histogram, mean relative to 0.5, chi-square with one degree of
  freedom; Monte Carlo Pi stays byte-driven).  -f folds upper-case
  letters (ASCII A-Z and Latin-1 0xC0-0xDE except 0xD7) to lower
  case in-line, with no scalar prepass.

  Outputs
  -------

  Human-readable text by default, CSV under -t, and JSON under
  --json.  -c adds a per-value occurrence table to any of them.
  -p / --full-precision renders every floating-point value at %.17g.

  Throughput
  ----------

  Banked SIMD histogram (four sub-bins per pass to break the
  read-modify-write hazard chain), serial-correlation cross-product
  via signed widened multiply + horizontal add (PMADDUBSW on
  SSE/AVX2, the same algorithm widened on AVX-512), bit-mode
  population count via VPOPCNTB on AVX-512 BITALG hosts and a
  PSHUFB nibble lookup elsewhere.  One binary runtime-dispatches
  scalar / SSSE3 / SSE4.1 / AVX2 / AVX-512 (F + BW + CD + DQ + VL
  + VPOPCNTDQ + BITALG) via a CPUID query; SIMD variants live in
  per-file static archives with isolated -m... CFLAGS.

  Regular-file inputs are memory-mapped with MADV_SEQUENTIAL +
  POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL.  Stdin and unmappable sources go through
  a 2 MiB read(2) loop; --no-mmap forces that path everywhere.

  -j N / --threads N partitions the mmap region across N pthread
  workers along 6-aligned slab boundaries so the Monte Carlo Pi
  state machine never crosses a thread, with adjacent slab
  products stitched into the serial-correlation sum at merge time.
  Output is byte-identical to the single-threaded run.  -j auto
  resolves to sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN) (GetSystemInfo on
  Windows).

  Platforms
  ---------

  Native builds: any C99 compiler with a working libc.  TCC
  compiles under --disable-threads.

  Cross-compile and pre-built binary support:

  - Linux musl: x86_64, i386, aarch64, armhf, riscv64, ppc64le,
    ppc64, ppc, s390x, loongarch64, mips, mipsel, mips64, mips64el.
  - Linux glibc: alpha, sparc64, sparc, m68k, hppa, arc, sh4.
  - Windows (mingw-w64): x86_64, i686, aarch64.
  - Windows 95: i686 with --with-windows-target=win95
    (kernel32 + msvcrt imports only, PE subsystem 4.0,
    no Unicode wide-API dependencies).
  - macOS (libSystem-stubbed): x86_64, aarch64.
  - MS-DOS via DJGPP: i386, with CWSDPMI baked into the .exe so
    no separate CWSDPMI.EXE is needed at runtime.

  Build system
  ------------

  GNU autotools.  ./bootstrap regenerates the autotools artefacts
  from configure.ac / Makefile.am.  ./configure --enable-native
  --enable-lto enables host-specific tuning and link-time
  optimisation.  --disable-threads drops the pthread dependency.
  --with-windows-target=vista|win95 selects the Windows target.

  Testing
  -------

  make check runs a deterministic-fixture sanity suite (fixtures
  live under $(builddir)/tests/fixtures so the source tree stays
  read-only).  make bench sweeps 10 datasets through three modes
  and a power-of-two -j ladder, with ent(1) timed alongside if it
  is on PATH; make bench-quick is the sub-minute smoke variant.
